messages:
olga: Heads up — sampleapp regen check failed after yesterday's auth tweak. Regendiff shows casing changes + reordered props, caused an unintended SDK bump.
ci-bot: [ci] https://ci.internal.redwood/teams/devex/pipelines/4620/builds/9934 — regen check failed :x:
ben: can you paste the snippet? suspect typegen map-iteration nondeterminism or a sanitizer slipped into fixtures.
olga: snippet:
---
-  "AuthOptions": {
-    "retry": {"maxAttempts": 3},
-    "useDefault": true
-  }
+  "AuthOptions": {
+    "use_default": true,
+    "retry": {"maxAttempts": 3}
+  }
---
-  "x-redwood-meta": {
-    "source": "auth-service"
-  }
+  "x_redwood_meta": {
+    "source": "auth-service"
+  }

ben: yep — normalizeJson from infra got pulled into a test helper and changed fixture keys. Also typegen wasn't sorting keys.
dara: plan: remove sanitizer from generator fixtures, add deterministic key sort in typegen emitter, add regen-stability test (run regen N times). Gate automatic publish: require label `sdk-release` to actually bump/publish.
olga: I'll revert the accidental package.json bump and add SKIP_AUTOPUBLISH=true in pipeline until the fix lands.
ben: PR 2540 opened with the revert + sort + tests. tagging devex + eng-runtime reviewers.
ci-bot: PR 2540 checks queued: regen + unit tests.
dara: once PR merges, run scripts/regenerate.sh && commit the clean regen, then re-enable publish gate and run smoke: https://smoke.internal.redwood/runs/5630
olga: thanks team — keeping pipeline blocked until we confirm clean regen.
